# Build artifacts — per-file IR, coverage, binaries — produced by bs2/bs3
# compile + link for any .av source. Covers tests/, packages/, src/.
**/*.av.ll
**/*.av.cov.ll
**/*.av.ll.cov.ll
**/*.av.covmap.json
**/*.bin
**/*.bin.o
**/*.profraw
**/*.profdata
# Per-pid atomic-materialise staging (`<artifact>.tmp.<pid>` — the
# tmp+rename discipline in link.av / llvm_wrapper.c / runtime.c). A
# killed process orphans its tmp beside tracked fixtures; transient
# by design, never source.
**/*.tmp.[0-9]*
# Ignore any directory named `build/` (catches the top-level artifact
# dir AND any per-package build/ such as packages/std-lsp/build/),
# but RE-INCLUDE the legitimate build-driver source module that lives
# at packages/std-avrac/src/build/.
**/build/
!packages/std-avrac/src/build/
!packages/std-avrac/src/build/**
# Per-file cache fingerprints — re-exclude inside the whitelisted source dir
packages/std-avrac/src/build/**/*.avra-sha256
# Build cache artifacts created when running builds from inside the package
# (e.g. `cd packages/std-avrac && bs2 build`) — NOT source, must stay ignored.
packages/std-avrac/src/build/cache/
# Test-run artifacts that land in the SAME directory as the build-driver source.
# The `!packages/std-avrac/src/build/**` re-include above exists for the .av SOURCE
# module, but it also un-ignores every artifact a run with cwd INSIDE the package
# drops here — which the blanket `**/build/` would otherwise have caught. A
# `bs2 test` from `packages/std-avrac/src` leaves per-CGU objects and a shard log
# right next to the source, and a plain `git add` over src/ then sweeps them into
# the commit (19 files, observed independently on #1077 and twice in one session
# on #1083 — caught on review both times, which is not a control).
packages/std-avrac/src/build/*.o
packages/std-avrac/src/build/test_shards/
packages/std-avrac/src/build/coverage/
packages/std-avrac/src/build/sweep/
packages/std-avrac/src/build/memguard/
dogfood_progress.csv

# Generated language reference (rebuild with 'avra lang')
target/
